    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0220" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/122: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Scott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-01T17:00:00-04:30">July 1, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Substance of Department’s circular telegrams of June 29, 4 p.m. and 6 p.m.
                    given Minister for Foreign Affairs,<anchor n="40" xml:id="d273-f1"/> who states
                    that it is doubtful if he can go to Havana. However, if Secretary Hull goes and
                    attendance of other Ministers of Foreign Affairs seems slight, he will make
                    every effort to go.</p>
                <pb facs="0221" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>
                <p>Revised agenda being studied and believed will be accepted by Venezuela without
                    changes. Venezuelan Embassy will be instructed by cable, July 3.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scott</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
